  "title": "Drought in India's South Peninsular Region and Rural Road Investments",
  "summary": "Tamil Nadu and Maharashtra are expected to face drought, with reports indicating relief measures are being announced. Meanwhile, the Centre allocated ₹1,000 crore for rural roads in West Bengal, while other regions like India are also investing in AI and connected vehicles, highlighting economic growth.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Tamil Nadu is expected to be among drought-hit taluks in India, with reports from the Hindu National indicating that the first list is not final.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maharashtra declared 265 taluks as drought-affected, including 74% of the state, and announced relief measures.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Centre allocated ₹1,000 crore under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana in the first phase for rural road construction.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
